#: erpnext/accounts/onboarding_step/accounts_settings/accounts_settings.json
#. Description of the Onboarding Step 'Accounts Settings'
msgid ""
"# Account Settings\n"
"\n"
"In ERPNext, Accounting features are configurable as per your business "
"needs. Accounts Settings is the place to define some of your accounting "
"preferences like:\n"
"\n"
" - Credit Limit and over billing settings\n"
" - Taxation preferences\n"
" - Deferred accounting preferences\n"
msgstr ""
"# Paramètres comptables\n"
"\n"
"Dans ERPNext, les fonctionnalités comptables sont configurables selon vos "
"besoins. Les paramètres comptables vous permettent de définir vos "
"préférences telles que :\n"
"\n"
" - Limite de crédit et paramètres de surfacturation\n"
" - Préférences fiscales\n"
" - Préférences de comptabilité différée\n"

#: erpnext/accounts/onboarding_step/configure_account_settings/configure_account_settings.json
#. Description of the Onboarding Step 'Configure Account Settings'
msgid ""
"# Account Settings\n"
"\n"
"This is a crucial piece of configuration. There are various account "
"settings in ERPNext to restrict and configure actions in the Accounting "
"module.\n"
"\n"
"The following settings are avaialble for you to configure\n"
"\n"
"1. Account Freezing \n"
"2. Credit and Overbilling\n"
"3. Invoicing and Tax Automations\n"
"4. Balance Sheet configurations\n"
"\n"
"There's much more, you can check it all out in this step"
msgstr ""
"# Paramètres comptables\n"
"\n"
"Ceci est un élément de configuration essentiel. Il existe divers paramètres "
"comptables dans ERPNext pour restreindre et configurer les actions du "
"module Comptabilité.\n"
"\n"
"Les paramètres suivants sont disponibles pour configuration\n"
"\n"
"1. Gel de compte \n"
"2. Crédit et surfacturation\n"
"3. Automatisations de facturation et fiscalité\n"
"4. Configurations du bilan\n"
"\n"
"Il y en a bien plus, vous pouvez tout découvrir dans cette étape"

#: erpnext/assets/onboarding_step/existing_asset/existing_asset.json
#. Description of the Onboarding Step 'Add an Existing Asset'
msgid ""
"# Add an Existing Asset\n"
"\n"
"If you are just starting with ERPNext, you will need to enter Assets you "
"already possess. You can add them as existing fixed assets in ERPNext. "
"Please note that you will have to make a Journal Entry separately updating "
"the opening balance in the fixed asset account."
msgstr ""
"# Ajouter un actif existant\n"
"\n"
"Si vous débutez avec ERPNext, vous devrez saisir les actifs que vous "
"possédez déjà. Vous pouvez les ajouter en tant qu'immobilisations "
"existantes dans ERPNext. Veuillez noter que vous devrez créer une écriture "
"comptable séparée pour mettre à jour le solde d'ouverture du compte "
"d'immobilisations."

#: erpnext/setup/onboarding_step/create_your_first_sales_invoice/create_your_first_sales_invoice.json
#. Description of the Onboarding Step 'Create Your First Sales Invoice '
msgid ""
"# All about sales invoice\n"
"\n"
"A Sales Invoice is a bill that you send to your Customers against which the "
"Customer makes the payment. Sales Invoice is an accounting transaction. On "
"submission of Sales Invoice, the system updates the receivable and books "
"income against a Customer Account."
msgstr ""
"# Tout sur la facture de vente\n"
"\n"
"Une facture de vente est une facture que vous envoyez à vos clients et sur "
"laquelle le client effectue le paiement. La facture de vente est une "
"transaction comptable. Lors de la soumission de la facture de vente, le "
"système met à jour les créances et enregistre le revenu sur le compte "
"client."

#: erpnext/accounts/onboarding_step/create_your_first_sales_invoice/create_your_first_sales_invoice.json
#. Description of the Onboarding Step 'Create Your First Sales Invoice '
msgid ""
"# All about sales invoice\n"
"\n"
"A Sales Invoice is a bill that you send to your Customers against which the "
"Customer makes the payment. Sales Invoice is an accounting transaction. On "
"submission of Sales Invoice, the system updates the receivable and books "
"income against a Customer Account.\n"
"\n"
"Here's the flow of how a sales invoice is generally created\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"![Sales Flow](https://docs.erpnext.com/docs/assets/img/accounts/so-flow.png)"
msgstr ""
"# Tout sur la facture de vente\n"
"\n"
"Une facture de vente est une facture que vous envoyez à vos clients et sur "
"laquelle le client effectue le paiement. La facture de vente est une "
"transaction comptable. Lors de la soumission de la facture de vente, le "
"système met à jour les créances et enregistre le revenu sur le compte "
"client.\n"
"\n"
"Voici le flux de création d'une facture de vente\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"![Flux de "
"vente](https://docs.erpnext.com/docs/assets/img/accounts/so-flow.png)"

#: erpnext/assets/onboarding_step/asset_category/asset_category.json
#. Description of the Onboarding Step 'Define Asset Category'
msgid ""
"# Asset Category\n"
"\n"
"An Asset Category classifies different assets of a Company.\n"
"\n"
"You can create an Asset Category based on the type of assets. For example, "
"all your desktops and laptops can be part of an Asset Category named "
"\"Electronic Equipments\". Create a separate category for furniture. Also, "
"you can update default properties for each category, like:\n"
" - Depreciation type and duration\n"
" - Fixed asset account\n"
" - Depreciation account\n"
msgstr ""
"# Catégorie d'actifs\n"
"\n"
"Une catégorie d'actifs classifie les différents actifs d'une entreprise.\n"
"\n"
"Vous pouvez créer une catégorie d'actifs basée sur le type d'actifs. Par "
"exemple, tous vos ordinateurs de bureau et portables peuvent faire partie "
"d'une catégorie d'actifs nommée \"Équipements électroniques\". Créez une "
"catégorie séparée pour le mobilier. Vous pouvez également mettre à jour les "
"propriétés par défaut de chaque catégorie, telles que :\n"
" - Type et durée d'amortissement\n"
" - Compte d'immobilisations\n"
" - Compte d'amortissement\n"

#: erpnext/assets/onboarding_step/asset_item/asset_item.json
#. Description of the Onboarding Step 'Create an Asset Item'
msgid ""
"# Asset Item\n"
"\n"
"Asset items are created based on Asset Category. You can create one or "
"multiple items against once Asset Category. The sales and purchase "
"transaction for Asset is done via Asset Item. "
msgstr ""
"# Article d'actif\n"
"\n"
"Les articles d'actif sont créés en fonction de la catégorie d'actifs. Vous "
"pouvez créer un ou plusieurs articles pour une catégorie d'actifs. Les "
"transactions de vente et d'achat d'actifs sont effectuées via l'article "
"d'actif."

#: erpnext/buying/onboarding_step/introduction_to_buying/introduction_to_buying.json
#. Description of the Onboarding Step 'Buying Settings'
msgid ""
"# Buying Settings\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Buying module’s features are highly configurable as per your business "
"needs. Buying Settings is the place where you can set your preferences for:\n"
"\n"
"- Supplier naming and default values\n"
"- Billing and shipping preference in buying transactions\n"
"\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#: erpnext/crm/onboarding_step/crm_settings/crm_settings.json
#. Description of the Onboarding Step 'CRM Settings'
msgid ""
"# CRM Settings\n"
"\n"
"CRM module’s features are configurable as per your business needs. CRM "
"Settings is the place where you can set your preferences for:\n"
"- Campaign\n"
"- Lead\n"
"- Opportunity\n"
"- Quotation"
msgstr ""

#: erpnext/accounts/onboarding_step/chart_of_accounts/chart_of_accounts.json
#. Description of the Onboarding Step 'Review Chart of Accounts'
msgid ""
"# Chart Of Accounts\n"
"\n"
"ERPNext sets up a simple chart of accounts for each Company you create, but "
"you can modify it according to business and legal requirements."
msgstr ""
"# Plan comptable\n"
"\n"
"ERPNext met en place un plan comptable simple pour chaque société que vous "
"créez, mais vous pouvez le modifier selon les exigences commerciales et "
"légales."

#: erpnext/stock/onboarding_step/check_stock_ledger_report/check_stock_ledger_report.json
#: erpnext/stock/onboarding_step/view_stock_projected_qty/view_stock_projected_qty.json
#. Description of the Onboarding Step 'Check Stock Ledger'
#. Description of the Onboarding Step 'Check Stock Projected Qty'
msgid ""
"# Check Stock Reports\n"
"Based on the various stock transactions, you can get a host of one-click "
"Stock Reports in ERPNext like Stock Ledger, Stock Balance, Projected "
"Quantity, and Ageing analysis."
msgstr ""
"# Consulter les rapports de stock\n"
"Sur la base des différentes transactions de stock, vous pouvez obtenir une "
"multitude de rapports de stock en un clic dans ERPNext, tels que le grand "
"livre de stock, le solde de stock, la quantité projetée et l'analyse "
"d'ancienneté."

#: erpnext/accounts/onboarding_step/cost_centers_for_report_and_budgeting/cost_centers_for_report_and_budgeting.json
#. Description of the Onboarding Step 'Cost Centers for Budgeting and Analysis'
msgid ""
"# Cost Centers for Budgeting and Analysis\n"
"\n"
"While your Books of Accounts are framed to fulfill statutory requirements, "
"you can set up Cost Center and Accounting Dimensions to address your "
"companies reporting and budgeting requirements.\n"
"\n"
"Click here to learn more about how  <b>[Cost "
"Center](https://docs.erpnext.com/docs/v13/user/manual/en/accounts/cost-"
"center)</b> and <b> "
"[Dimensions](https://docs.erpnext.com/docs/v13/user/manual/en/accounts/"
"accounting-dimensions)</b> allow you to get advanced financial analytics "
"reports from ERPNext."
msgstr ""
"# Centres de coûts pour la budgétisation et l'analyse\n"
"\n"
"Bien que vos livres comptables soient conçus pour répondre aux exigences "
"légales, vous pouvez configurer des centres de coûts et des dimensions "
"comptables pour répondre aux besoins de reporting et de budgétisation de "
"votre entreprise.\n"
"\n"
"Cliquez ici pour en savoir plus sur la façon dont les <b>[Centres de "
"coûts](https://docs.erpnext.com/docs/v13/user/manual/en/accounts/cost-"
"center)</b> et les "
"<b>[Dimensions](https://docs.erpnext.com/docs/v13/user/manual/en/accounts/"
"accounting-dimensions)</b> vous permettent d'obtenir des rapports d'analyse "
"financière avancés depuis ERPNext."

#: erpnext/manufacturing/onboarding_step/create_product/create_product.json
#. Description of the Onboarding Step 'Finished Items'
msgid ""
"# Create Items for Bill of Materials\n"
"\n"
"One of the prerequisites of a BOM is the creation of raw materials, "
"sub-assembly, and finished items. Once these items are created, you will be "
"able to proceed to the Bill of Materials master, which is composed of items "
"and routing.\n"
msgstr ""
"# Créer des articles pour la nomenclature\n"
"\n"
"L'un des prérequis d'une nomenclature est la création de matières "
"premières, de sous-ensembles et d'articles finis. Une fois ces articles "
"créés, vous pourrez accéder au formulaire de nomenclature, qui est composé "
"d'articles et de gammes opératoires.\n"

#: erpnext/manufacturing/onboarding_step/operation/operation.json
#. Description of the Onboarding Step 'Operation'
msgid ""
"# Create Operations\n"
"\n"
"An Operation refers to any manufacturing operation performed on the raw "
"materials to process it further in the manufacturing path. As an example, "
"if you are into garments manufacturing, you will create Operations like "
"fabric cutting, stitching, and washing as some of the operations."
msgstr ""
"# Créer des opérations\n"
"\n"
"Une opération fait référence à toute opération de fabrication effectuée sur "
"les matières premières pour les transformer dans le processus de "
"fabrication. Par exemple, si vous êtes dans la fabrication de vêtements, "
"vous créerez des opérations telles que la coupe du tissu, la couture et le "
"lavage."

#: erpnext/manufacturing/onboarding_step/workstation/workstation.json
#. Description of the Onboarding Step 'Workstation'
msgid ""
"# Create Workstations\n"
"\n"
"A Workstation stores information regarding the place where the workstation "
"operations are performed. As an example, if you have ten sewing machines "
"doing stitching jobs, each machine will be added as a workstation."
msgstr ""
"# Créer des postes de travail\n"
"\n"
"Un poste de travail stocke les informations relatives à l'endroit où les "
"opérations sont effectuées. Par exemple, si vous avez dix machines à coudre "
"effectuant des travaux de couture, chaque machine sera ajoutée comme poste "
"de travail."

#: erpnext/manufacturing/onboarding_step/create_bom/create_bom.json
#. Description of the Onboarding Step 'Bill of Materials'
msgid ""
"# Create a Bill of Materials\n"
"\n"
"A Bill of Materials (BOM) is a list of items and sub-assemblies with "
"quantities required to manufacture an Item.\n"
"\n"
"BOM also provides cost estimation for the production of the item. It takes "
"raw-materials cost based on valuation and operations to cost based on "
"routing, which gives total costing for a BOM."
msgstr ""
"# Créer une nomenclature\n"
"\n"
"Une nomenclature (BOM) est une liste d'articles et de sous-ensembles avec "
"les quantités nécessaires à la fabrication d'un article.\n"
"\n"
"La nomenclature fournit également une estimation des coûts pour la "
"production de l'article. Elle prend en compte le coût des matières "
"premières basé sur la valorisation et les opérations de coût basées sur la "
"gamme, ce qui donne le coût total d'une nomenclature."

#: erpnext/setup/onboarding_step/create_a_customer/create_a_customer.json
#. Description of the Onboarding Step 'Create a Customer'
msgid ""
"# Create a Customer\n"
"\n"
"The Customer master is at the heart of your sales transactions. Customers "
"are linked in Quotations, Sales Orders, Invoices, and Payments. Customers "
"can be either numbered or identified by name (you would typically do this "
"based on the number of customers you have).\n"
"\n"
"Through Customer’s master, you can effectively track essentials like:\n"
" - Customer’s multiple address and contacts\n"
" - Account Receivables\n"
" - Credit Limit and Credit Period\n"
msgstr ""

#: erpnext/setup/onboarding_step/letterhead/letterhead.json
#. Description of the Onboarding Step 'Setup Your Letterhead'
msgid ""
"# Create a Letter Head\n"
"\n"
"A Letter Head contains your organization's name, logo, address, etc which "
"appears at the header and footer portion in documents. You can learn more "
"about Setting up Letter Head in ERPNext here.\n"
msgstr ""
"# Créer un en-tête\n"
"\n"
"Un en-tête contient le nom, le logo, l'adresse de votre organisation, etc., "
"qui apparaît dans la partie en-tête et pied de page des documents. Vous "
"pouvez en savoir plus sur la configuration des en-têtes dans ERPNext ici.\n"

#: erpnext/setup/onboarding_step/create_a_quotation/create_a_quotation.json
#. Description of the Onboarding Step 'Create your first Quotation'
msgid ""
"# Create a Quotation\n"
"\n"
"Let’s get started with business transactions by creating your first "
"Quotation. You can create a Quotation for an existing customer or a "
"prospect. It will be an approved document, with items you sell and the "
"proposed price + taxes applied. After completing the instructions, you will "
"get a Quotation in a ready to share print format."
msgstr ""

#: erpnext/setup/onboarding_step/create_a_supplier/create_a_supplier.json
#. Description of the Onboarding Step 'Create a Supplier'
msgid ""
"# Create a Supplier\n"
"\n"
"Also known as Vendor, is a master at the center of your purchase "
"transactions. Suppliers are linked in Request for Quotation, Purchase "
"Orders, Receipts, and Payments. Suppliers can be either numbered or "
"identified by name.\n"
"\n"
"Through Supplier’s master, you can effectively track essentials like:\n"
" - Supplier’s multiple address and contacts\n"
" - Account Receivables\n"
" - Credit Limit and Credit Period\n"
msgstr ""

#: erpnext/stock/onboarding_step/create_a_supplier/create_a_supplier.json
#. Description of the Onboarding Step 'Create a Supplier'
msgid ""
"# Create a Supplier\n"
"In this step we will create a **Supplier**. If you have already created a "
"**Supplier** you can skip this step."
msgstr ""
"# Créer un fournisseur\n"
"Dans cette étape, nous allons créer un **Fournisseur**. Si vous avez déjà "
"créé un **Fournisseur**, vous pouvez ignorer cette étape."

#: erpnext/manufacturing/onboarding_step/work_order/work_order.json
#. Description of the Onboarding Step 'Work Order'
msgid ""
"# Create a Work Order\n"
"\n"
"A Work Order or a Job order is given to the manufacturing shop floor by the "
"Production Manager to initiate the manufacturing of a certain quantity of "
"an item. Work Order carriers details of production Item, its BOM, "
"quantities to be manufactured, and operations.\n"
"\n"
"Through Work Order, you can track various production status like:\n"
"\n"
"- Issue of raw-material to shop material\n"
"- Progress on each Workstation via Job Card\n"
"- Manufactured Quantity against Work Order\n"
msgstr ""
"# Créer un ordre de fabrication\n"
"\n"
"Un ordre de fabrication est transmis à l'atelier de production par le "
"responsable de production pour initier la fabrication d'une certaine "
"quantité d'un article. L'ordre de fabrication contient les détails de "
"l'article à produire, sa nomenclature, les quantités à fabriquer et les "
"opérations.\n"
"\n"
"Grâce à l'ordre de fabrication, vous pouvez suivre divers statuts de "
"production tels que :\n"
"\n"
"- Sortie de matières premières vers l'atelier\n"
"- Avancement sur chaque poste de travail via la fiche de travail\n"
"- Quantité fabriquée par rapport à l'ordre de fabrication\n"

#: erpnext/setup/onboarding_step/create_an_item/create_an_item.json
#. Description of the Onboarding Step 'Create an Item'
msgid ""
"# Create an Item\n"
"\n"
"Item is a product or a service offered by your company, or something you "
"buy as a part of your supplies or raw materials.\n"
"\n"
"Items are integral to everything you do in ERPNext - from billing, "
"purchasing to managing inventory. Everything you buy or sell, whether it is "
"a physical product or a service is an Item. Items can be stock, non-stock, "
"variants, serialized, batched, assets, etc.\n"
msgstr ""
"# Créer un article\n"
"\n"
"Un article est un produit ou un service proposé par votre entreprise, ou "
"quelque chose que vous achetez dans le cadre de vos fournitures ou matières "
"premières.\n"
"\n"
"Les articles sont au cœur de tout ce que vous faites dans ERPNext - de la "
"facturation aux achats en passant par la gestion des stocks. Tout ce que "
"vous achetez ou vendez, qu'il s'agisse d'un produit physique ou d'un "
"service, est un article. Les articles peuvent être stockés, non stockés, "
"des variantes, sérialisés, par lots, des actifs, etc.\n"

#: erpnext/stock/onboarding_step/create_an_item/create_an_item.json
#. Description of the Onboarding Step 'Create an Item'
msgid ""
"# Create an Item\n"
"The Stock module deals with the movement of items.\n"
"\n"
"In this step we will create an  "
"[**Item**](https://docs.erpnext.com/docs/user/manual/en/stock/item)."
msgstr ""
"# Créer un article\n"
"Le module Stock gère le mouvement des articles.\n"
"\n"
"Dans cette étape, nous allons créer un "
"[**Article**](https://docs.erpnext.com/docs/user/manual/en/stock/item)."

#: erpnext/buying/onboarding_step/create_your_first_purchase_order/create_your_first_purchase_order.json
#. Description of the Onboarding Step 'Create first Purchase Order'
msgid ""
"# Create first Purchase Order\n"
"\n"
"Purchase Order is at the heart of your buying transactions. In ERPNext, "
"Purchase Order can can be created against a Purchase Material Request "
"(indent) and Supplier Quotation as well.  Purchase Orders is also linked to "
"Purchase Receipt and Purchase Invoices, allowing you to keep a birds-eye "
"view on your purchase deals.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"# Créer votre premier bon de commande\n"
"\n"
"Le bon de commande est au cœur de vos transactions d'achat. Dans ERPNext, "
"un bon de commande peut être créé à partir d'une demande de matériel "
"d'achat (réquisition) et d'un devis fournisseur. Les bons de commande sont "
"également liés aux reçus d'achat et factures d'achat, vous permettant de "
"garder une vue d'ensemble sur vos achats.\n"
"\n"

#: erpnext/accounts/onboarding_step/create_your_first_purchase_invoice/create_your_first_purchase_invoice.json
#. Description of the Onboarding Step 'Create Your First Purchase Invoice '
msgid ""
"# Create your first Purchase Invoice\n"
"\n"
"A Purchase Invoice is a bill received from a Supplier for a product(s) or "
"service(s) delivery to your company. You can track payables through "
"Purchase Invoice and process Payment Entries against it.\n"
"\n"
"Purchase Invoices can also be created against a Purchase Order or Purchase "
"Receipt."
msgstr ""
"# Créer votre première facture d'achat\n"
"\n"
"Une facture d'achat est une facture reçue d'un fournisseur pour la "
"livraison de produit(s) ou service(s) à votre entreprise. Vous pouvez "
"suivre les comptes fournisseurs via la facture d'achat et traiter les "
"écritures de paiement correspondantes.\n"
"\n"
"Les factures d'achat peuvent également être créées à partir d'un bon de "
"commande ou d'un reçu d'achat."

#: erpnext/accounts/onboarding_step/financial_statements/financial_statements.json
#. Description of the Onboarding Step 'Financial Statements'
msgid ""
"# Financial Statements\n"
"\n"
"In ERPNext, you can get crucial financial reports like [Balance Sheet] and "
"[Profit and Loss] statements with a click of a button. You can run in the "
"report for a different period and plot analytics charts premised on "
"statement data. For more reports, check sections like Financial Statements, "
"General Ledger, and Profitability reports.\n"
"\n"
"<b>[Check Accounting "
"reports](https://docs.erpnext.com/docs/v13/user/manual/en/accounts/"
"accounting-reports)</b>"
msgstr ""
"# États financiers\n"
"\n"
"Dans ERPNext, vous pouvez obtenir des rapports financiers essentiels comme "
"le [Bilan] et le [Compte de résultat] en un clic. Vous pouvez exécuter le "
"rapport pour une période différente et tracer des graphiques analytiques "
"basés sur les données des états. Pour plus de rapports, consultez les "
"sections telles que États financiers, Grand livre et rapports de "
"rentabilité.\n"
"\n"
"<b>[Consulter les rapports "
"comptables](https://docs.erpnext.com/docs/v13/user/manual/en/accounts/"
"accounting-reports)</b>"

#: erpnext/assets/onboarding_step/fixed_asset_accounts/fixed_asset_accounts.json
#. Description of the Onboarding Step 'Review Fixed Asset Accounts'
msgid ""
"# Fixed Asset Accounts\n"
"\n"
"With the company, a host of fixed asset accounts are pre-configured. To "
"ensure your asset transactions are leading to correct accounting entries, "
"you can review and set up following asset accounts as per your business  "
"requirements.\n"
" - Fixed asset accounts (Asset account)\n"
" - Accumulated depreciation\n"
" - Capital Work in progress (CWIP) account\n"
" - Asset Depreciation account (Expense account)"
msgstr ""
"# Comptes d'immobilisations\n"
"\n"
"Avec la société, un ensemble de comptes d'immobilisations sont "
"préconfigurés. Pour vous assurer que vos transactions d'actifs génèrent des "
"écritures comptables correctes, vous pouvez vérifier et configurer les "
"comptes d'actifs suivants selon vos besoins :\n"
" - Comptes d'immobilisations (compte d'actif)\n"
" - Amortissements cumulés\n"
" - Compte d'immobilisations en cours (CWIP)\n"
" - Compte d'amortissement des actifs (compte de charges)"

#: erpnext/manufacturing/onboarding_step/production_planning/production_planning.json
#. Description of the Onboarding Step 'Production Planning'
msgid ""
"# How Production Planning Works\n"
"\n"
"Production Plan helps in production and material planning for the Items "
"planned for manufacturing. These production items can be committed via "
"Sales Order (to Customers) or Material Requests (internally).\n"
msgstr ""
"# Comment fonctionne la planification de production\n"
"\n"
"Le plan de production aide à la planification de la production et des "
"matériaux pour les articles prévus en fabrication. Ces articles de "
"production peuvent être engagés via des commandes clients (pour les "
"clients) ou des demandes de matériel (en interne).\n"

#: erpnext/setup/onboarding_step/data_import/data_import.json
#. Description of the Onboarding Step 'Import Data from Spreadsheet'
msgid ""
"# Import Data from Spreadsheet\n"
"\n"
"In ERPNext, you can easily migrate your historical data using spreadsheets. "
"You can use it for migrating not just masters (like Customer, Supplier, "
"Items), but also for transactions like (outstanding invoices, opening stock "
"and accounting entries, etc)."
msgstr ""
"# Importer des données depuis un tableur\n"
"\n"
"Dans ERPNext, vous pouvez facilement migrer vos données historiques à "
"l'aide de tableurs. Vous pouvez l'utiliser pour migrer non seulement les "
"données de base (comme les clients, fournisseurs, articles), mais aussi les "
"transactions (factures impayées, stock d'ouverture et écritures comptables, "
"etc.)."

#: erpnext/manufacturing/report/work_order_stock_report/work_order_stock_report.py:148
msgid "# In Stock"
msgstr "# En stock"

#: erpnext/stock/onboarding_step/introduction_to_stock_entry/introduction_to_stock_entry.json
#. Description of the Onboarding Step 'Introduction to Stock Entry'
msgid ""
"# Introduction to Stock Entry\n"
"This video will give a quick introduction to [**Stock "
"Entry**](https://docs.erpnext.com/docs/user/manual/en/stock/stock-entry)."
msgstr ""
"# Introduction à l'écriture de stock\n"
"Cette vidéo vous donnera une introduction rapide à l'[**Écriture de "
"stock**](https://docs.erpnext.com/docs/user/manual/en/stock/stock-entry)."

#: erpnext/stock/onboarding_step/create_a_stock_entry/create_a_stock_entry.json
#. Description of the Onboarding Step 'Manage Stock Movements'
msgid ""
"# Manage Stock Movements\n"
"Stock entry allows you to register the movement of stock for various "
"purposes like transfer, received, issues, repacked, etc. To address issues "
"related to theft and pilferages,  you can always ensure that the movement "
"of goods happens against a document reference Stock Entry in ERPNext.\n"
"\n"
"Let’s get a quick walk-through on the various scenarios covered in Stock "
"Entry by watching [*this "
"video*](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Njt107hlY3I)."
msgstr ""

#: erpnext/setup/onboarding_step/navigation_help/navigation_help.json
#. Description of the Onboarding Step 'How to Navigate in ERPNext'
msgid ""
"# Navigation in ERPNext\n"
"\n"
"Ease of navigating and browsing around the ERPNext is one of our core "
"strengths. In the following video, you will learn how to reach a specific "
"feature in ERPNext via module page or AwesomeBar."
msgstr ""
"# Navigation dans ERPNext\n"
"\n"
"La facilité de navigation dans ERPNext est l'un de nos points forts. Dans "
"la vidéo suivante, vous apprendrez comment accéder à une fonctionnalité "
"spécifique dans ERPNext via la page de module ou la barre de recherche."

#: erpnext/assets/onboarding_step/asset_purchase/asset_purchase.json
#. Description of the Onboarding Step 'Purchase an Asset'
msgid ""
"# Purchase an Asset\n"
"\n"
"Assets purchases process if done following the standard Purchase cycle. If "
"capital work in progress is enabled in Asset Category, Asset will be "
"created as soon as Purchase Receipt is created for it. You can quickly "
"create a Purchase Receipt for Asset and see its impact on books of accounts."
msgstr ""
"# Acheter un actif\n"
"\n"
"Le processus d'achat d'actifs suit le cycle d'achat standard. Si le travail "
"en cours d'immobilisation est activé dans la catégorie d'actifs, l'actif "
"sera créé dès que le reçu d'achat sera créé. Vous pouvez rapidement créer "
"un reçu d'achat pour un actif et voir son impact sur les livres comptables."

#: erpnext/manufacturing/report/work_order_stock_report/work_order_stock_report.py:141
msgid "# Req'd Items"
msgstr "# Articles requis"

#: erpnext/manufacturing/onboarding_step/explore_manufacturing_settings/explore_manufacturing_settings.json
#. Description of the Onboarding Step 'Manufacturing Settings'
msgid ""
"# Review Manufacturing Settings\n"
"\n"
"In ERPNext, the Manufacturing module’s features are configurable as per "
"your business needs. Manufacturing Settings is the place where you can set "
"your preferences for:\n"
"\n"
"- Capacity planning for allocating jobs to workstations\n"
"- Raw-material consumption based on BOM or actual\n"
"- Default values and over-production allowance\n"
msgstr ""

#: erpnext/stock/onboarding_step/stock_settings/stock_settings.json
#. Description of the Onboarding Step 'Review Stock Settings'
msgid ""
"# Review Stock Settings\n"
"\n"
"In ERPNext, the Stock module’s features are configurable as per your "
"business needs. Stock Settings is the place where you can set your "
"preferences for:\n"
"- Default values for Item and Pricing\n"
"- Default valuation method for inventory valuation\n"
"- Set preference for serialization and batching of item\n"
"- Set tolerance for over-receipt and delivery of items"
msgstr ""

#: erpnext/selling/onboarding_step/sales_order/sales_order.json
#. Description of the Onboarding Step 'Sales Order'
msgid ""
"# Sales Order\n"
"\n"
"A Sales Order is a confirmation of an order from your customer. It is also "
"referred to as Proforma Invoice.\n"
"\n"
"Sales Order at the heart of your sales and purchase transactions. Sales "
"Orders are linked in Delivery Note, Sales Invoices, Material Request, and "
"Maintenance transactions. Through Sales Order, you can track fulfillment of "
"the overall deal towards the customer."
msgstr ""
"# Commande client\n"
"\n"
"Une commande client est une confirmation de commande de votre client. Elle "
"est également appelée facture pro forma.\n"
"\n"
"La commande client est au cœur de vos transactions de vente et d'achat. Les "
"commandes clients sont liées aux bons de livraison, factures de vente, "
"demandes de matériel et transactions de maintenance. Grâce à la commande "
"client, vous pouvez suivre l'exécution de l'ensemble de la transaction "
"envers le client."

#: erpnext/selling/onboarding_step/selling_settings/selling_settings.json
#. Description of the Onboarding Step 'Selling Settings'
msgid ""
"# Selling Settings\n"
"\n"
"CRM and Selling module’s features are configurable as per your business "
"needs. Selling Settings is the place where you can set your preferences "
"for:\n"
" - Customer naming and default values\n"
" - Billing and shipping preference in sales transactions\n"
msgstr ""

#: erpnext/setup/onboarding_step/company_set_up/company_set_up.json
#. Description of the Onboarding Step 'Set Up a Company'
msgid ""
"# Set Up a Company\n"
"\n"
"A company is a legal entity for which you will set up your books of account "
"and create accounting transactions. In ERPNext, you can create multiple "
"companies, and establish relationships (group/subsidiary) among them.\n"
"\n"
"Within the company master, you can capture various default accounts for "
"that Company and set crucial settings related to the accounting methodology "
"followed for a company.\n"
msgstr ""
"# Configurer une société\n"
"\n"
"Une société est une entité juridique pour laquelle vous allez configurer "
"vos livres comptables et créer des transactions comptables. Dans ERPNext, "
"vous pouvez créer plusieurs sociétés et établir des relations "
"(groupe/filiale) entre elles.\n"
"\n"
"Dans la fiche société, vous pouvez définir divers comptes par défaut pour "
"cette société et configurer des paramètres essentiels liés à la "
"méthodologie comptable suivie.\n"

#: erpnext/accounts/onboarding_step/setup_taxes/setup_taxes.json
#. Description of the Onboarding Step 'Setting up Taxes'
msgid ""
"# Setting up Taxes\n"
"\n"
"ERPNext lets you configure your taxes so that they are automatically "
"applied in your buying and selling transactions. You can configure them "
"globally or even on Items. ERPNext taxes are pre-configured for most "
"regions."
msgstr ""
"# Configuration des taxes\n"
"\n"
"ERPNext vous permet de configurer vos taxes afin qu'elles soient "
"automatiquement appliquées dans vos transactions d'achat et de vente. Vous "
"pouvez les configurer globalement ou même par article. Les taxes ERPNext "
"sont préconfigurées pour la plupart des régions."

#: erpnext/manufacturing/onboarding_step/routing/routing.json
#. Description of the Onboarding Step 'Routing'
msgid ""
"# Setup Routing\n"
"\n"
"A Routing stores all Operations along with the description, hourly rate, "
"operation time, batch size, etc. Click below to learn how the Routing "
"template can be created, for quick selection in the BOM."
msgstr ""
"# Configurer les gammes opératoires\n"
"\n"
"Une gamme opératoire stocke toutes les opérations ainsi que la description, "
"le taux horaire, le temps d'opération, la taille du lot, etc. Cliquez "
"ci-dessous pour apprendre comment créer un modèle de gamme opératoire pour "
"une sélection rapide dans la nomenclature."

#: erpnext/stock/onboarding_step/create_a_warehouse/create_a_warehouse.json
#. Description of the Onboarding Step 'Setup a Warehouse'
msgid ""
"# Setup a Warehouse\n"
"The warehouse can be your location/godown/store where you maintain the "
"item's inventory, and receive/deliver them to various parties.\n"
"\n"
"In ERPNext, you can maintain a Warehouse in the tree structure, so that "
"location and sub-location of an item can be tracked. Also, you can link a "
"Warehouse to a specific Accounting ledger, where the real-time stock value "
"of that warehouse’s item will be reflected."
msgstr ""

#: erpnext/buying/onboarding_step/create_a_material_request/create_a_material_request.json
#. Description of the Onboarding Step 'Track Material Request'
msgid ""
"# Track Material Request\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Also known as Purchase Request or an Indent, is a document identifying a "
"requirement of a set of items (products or services) for various purposes "
"like procurement, transfer, issue, or manufacturing. Once the Material "
"Request is validated, a purchase manager can take the next actions for "
"purchasing items like requesting RFQ from a supplier or directly placing an "
"order with an identified Supplier.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"# Suivre les demandes de matériel\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Également connue sous le nom de demande d'achat ou réquisition, c'est un "
"document identifiant un besoin pour un ensemble d'articles (produits ou "
"services) à diverses fins telles que l'approvisionnement, le transfert, la "
"sortie ou la fabrication. Une fois la demande de matériel validée, un "
"responsable des achats peut prendre les actions suivantes pour l'achat "
"d'articles, comme demander un appel d'offres à un fournisseur ou passer "
"directement une commande auprès d'un fournisseur identifié.\n"
"\n"

#: erpnext/stock/onboarding_step/stock_opening_balance/stock_opening_balance.json
#. Description of the Onboarding Step 'Update Stock Opening Balance'
msgid ""
"# Update Stock Opening Balance\n"
"It’s an entry to update the stock balance of an item, in a warehouse, on a "
"date and time you are going live on ERPNext.\n"
"\n"
"Once opening stocks are updated, you can create transactions like "
"manufacturing and stock deliveries, where this opening stock will be "
"consumed."
msgstr ""

#: erpnext/accounts/onboarding_step/updating_opening_balances/updating_opening_balances.json
#. Description of the Onboarding Step 'Updating Opening Balances'
msgid ""
"# Updating Opening Balances\n"
"\n"
"Once you close the financial statement in previous accounting software, you "
"can update the same as opening in your ERPNext's Balance Sheet accounts. "
"This will allow you to get complete financial statements from ERPNext in "
"the coming years, and discontinue the parallel accounting system right away."
msgstr ""
"# Mise à jour des soldes d'ouverture\n"
"\n"
"Une fois que vous clôturez les états financiers dans votre logiciel "
"comptable précédent, vous pouvez les saisir comme soldes d'ouverture dans "
"les comptes du bilan d'ERPNext. Cela vous permettra d'obtenir des états "
"financiers complets depuis ERPNext dans les années à venir et d'abandonner "
"immédiatement le système comptable parallèle."

#: erpnext/stock/onboarding_step/view_warehouses/view_warehouses.json
#. Description of the Onboarding Step 'View Warehouses'
msgid ""
"# View Warehouse\n"
"In ERPNext the term 'warehouse' can be thought of as a storage location.\n"
"\n"
"Warehouses are arranged in ERPNext in a tree like structure, where multiple "
"sub-warehouses can be grouped under a single warehouse.\n"
"\n"
"In this step we will view the [**Warehouse "
"Tree**](https://docs.erpnext.com/docs/user/manual/en/stock/warehouse#21-"
"tree-view) to view the "
"[**Warehouses**](https://docs.erpnext.com/docs/user/manual/en/stock/"
"warehouse) that are set by default."
msgstr ""
"# Voir les entrepôts\n"
"Dans ERPNext, le terme 'entrepôt' peut être considéré comme un emplacement "
"de stockage.\n"
"\n"
"Les entrepôts sont organisés dans ERPNext en structure arborescente, où "
"plusieurs sous-entrepôts peuvent être regroupés sous un seul entrepôt.\n"
"\n"
"Dans cette étape, nous allons voir l'[**Arborescence des "
"entrepôts**](https://docs.erpnext.com/docs/user/manual/en/stock/warehouse#21"
"-tree-view) pour voir les "
"[**Entrepôts**](https://docs.erpnext.com/docs/user/manual/en/stock/"
"warehouse) configurés par défaut."

#: erpnext/accounts/onboarding_step/create_a_product/create_a_product.json
#. Description of the Onboarding Step 'Create a Sales Item'
msgid ""
"## Products and Services\n"
"\n"
"Depending on the nature of your business, you might be selling products or "
"services to your clients or even both. \n"
"ERPNext is optimized for itemized management of your sales and purchase.\n"
"\n"
"The **Item Master**  is where you can add all your sales items. If you are "
"in services, you can create an Item for each service that you offer. If you "
"run a manufacturing business, the same master is used for keeping a record "
"of raw materials, sub-assemblies etc.\n"
"\n"
"Completing the Item Master is very essential for the successful "
"implementation of ERPNext. We have a brief video introducing the item "
"master for you, you can watch it in the next step."
msgstr ""
"## Produits et services\n"
"\n"
"Selon la nature de votre activité, vous pourriez vendre des produits ou des "
"services à vos clients, ou même les deux.\n"
"ERPNext est optimisé pour la gestion détaillée de vos ventes et achats.\n"
"\n"
"La **Fiche article** est l'endroit où vous pouvez ajouter tous vos articles "
"de vente. Si vous êtes dans les services, vous pouvez créer un article pour "
"chaque service que vous proposez. Si vous gérez une entreprise de "
"fabrication, la même fiche est utilisée pour tenir un registre des matières "
"premières, sous-ensembles, etc.\n"
"\n"
"Compléter la fiche article est essentiel pour la réussite de "
"l'implémentation d'ERPNext. Nous avons une brève vidéo présentant la fiche "
"article, que vous pouvez regarder à l'étape suivante."

#: erpnext/accounts/onboarding_step/create_a_customer/create_a_customer.json
#. Description of the Onboarding Step 'Create a Customer'
msgid ""
"## Who is a Customer?\n"
"\n"
"A customer, who is sometimes known as a client, buyer, or purchaser is the "
"one who receives goods, services, products, or ideas, from a seller for a "
"monetary consideration.\n"
"\n"
"Every customer needs to be assigned a unique id. Customer name itself can "
"be the id or you can set a naming series for ids to be generated in Selling "
"Settings.\n"
"\n"
"Just like the supplier, let's quickly create a customer."
msgstr ""
"## Qu'est-ce qu'un client ?\n"
"\n"
"Un client, parfois appelé acheteur, est celui qui reçoit des biens, "
"services, produits ou idées d'un vendeur contre une contrepartie monétaire.\n"
"\n"
"Chaque client doit se voir attribuer un identifiant unique. Le nom du "
"client peut lui-même être l'identifiant ou vous pouvez définir une série de "
"nommage pour générer les identifiants dans les paramètres de vente.\n"
"\n"
"Tout comme le fournisseur, créons rapidement un client."

#: erpnext/accounts/onboarding_step/create_a_supplier/create_a_supplier.json
#. Description of the Onboarding Step 'Create a Supplier'
msgid ""
"## Who is a Supplier?\n"
"\n"
"Suppliers are companies or individuals who provide you with products or "
"services. ERPNext has comprehensive features for purchase cycles. \n"
"\n"
"Let's quickly create a supplier with the minimal details required. You need "
"the name of the supplier, assign the supplier to a group, and select the "
"type of the supplier, viz. Company or Individual."
msgstr ""
"## Qu'est-ce qu'un fournisseur ?\n"
"\n"
"Les fournisseurs sont des entreprises ou des individus qui vous fournissent "
"des produits ou des services. ERPNext dispose de fonctionnalités complètes "
"pour les cycles d'achat.\n"
"\n"
"Créons rapidement un fournisseur avec les détails minimaux requis. Vous "
"avez besoin du nom du fournisseur, de l'assigner à un groupe et de "
"sélectionner le type du fournisseur, à savoir Société ou Individu."

